/*
 * [Branch & Defect Analysis Matrix]
 * 
 * Target: TypeValidator.java
 * 
 * Key branches and conditions to cover:
 * 1. expectObject: type.matchesObjectContext() true/false
 * 2. expectActualObject: type.isObject() true/false
 * 3. expectAnyObject: anyObjectType.isSubtype(type) && !type.isEmptyType()
 * 4. expectString: type.matchesStringContext() true/false
 * 5. expectNumber: type.matchesNumberContext() true/false
 * 6. expectBitwiseable: !type.matchesNumberContext() && !type.isSubtype(allValueTypes)
 * 7. expectStringOrNumber: !type.matchesNumberContext() && !type.matchesStringContext()
 * 8. expectNotNullOrUndefined: complex condition with isNoType, isUnknownType, isSubtype, containsForwardDeclaredUnresolvedName
 * 9. containsForwardDeclaredUnresolvedName: union type recursion, isNoResolvedType
 * 10. expectSwitchMatchesCase: canTestForShallowEqualityWith, autoboxesTo
 * 11. expectIndexMatch: isStruct, isUnknownType, dereferenced.getIndexType, isArrayType, matchesObjectContext
 * 12. expectCanAssignToPropertyOf: leftType.isNoType, rightType.canAssignTo, constructor/enum check, function prototype interface check
 * 13. expectCanAssignTo: rightType.canAssignTo, constructor/enum check
 * 14. expectArgumentMatchesParameter: argType.canAssignTo(paramType)
 * 15. expectCanOverride: overridingType.canAssignTo(hiddenType)
 * 16. expectSuperType: declaredSuper null check, UnknownType check, isEquivalentTo, OBJECT_TYPE check, subCtor.hasCachedValues
 * 17. expectCanCast: restrictByNotNullOrUndefined, canAssignTo both directions
 * 18. expectUndeclaredVariable: n.isGetProp, NodeUtil.isObjectLitKey, info null, suppressions contains duplicate, varType null/UNKNOWN, newType null/UNKNOWN, var.input null, parent.isVar, parent.isFunction, allowDupe, isExprResult, newType.isEquivalentTo
 * 19. expectAllInterfaceProperties: getAllImplementedInterfaces, getImplicitPrototype null, getOwnPropertyNames
 * 20. expectInterfaceProperty: propSlot null, propNode null, found.canAssignTo(required)
 * 21. mismatch overloads: NodeTraversal vs sourceName, JSType vs JSTypeNative
 * 22. registerMismatch: restrictByNotNullOrUndefined, canAssignTo both directions, function type parameter/return recursion
 * 23. registerIfMismatch: found/required null checks
 * 24. formatFoundRequired: MessageFormat
 * 25. getReadableJSTypeName: isGetProp, objectType null, constructor interface, while loop for prototype chain, function prototype type, dereference, qualifiedName null, isFunctionType
 * 26. getJSType: jsType null -> UNKNOWN_TYPE
 * 27. report: shouldReport true/false
 * 28. TypeMismatch: equals (both orderings), hashCode, toString
 * 
 * Defect targeting:
 * - testTypeRedefinition: expectUndeclaredVariable with enum type redefinition
 *   The bug is in the condition checking for duplicate variable declarations.
 *   When a variable is redefined with a different type (e.g., enum vs function),
 *   the warning should be reported. The defect causes the warning to be suppressed
 *   or the count to be wrong.
 * 
 * - testIssue635b: Related to type checking of property access on struct types
 *   in expectIndexMatch, where ILLEGAL_PROPERTY_ACCESS should be reported.
 */
